  "body": "What happens:\nRotary Parallel does not cut all the way around the cylinder circumference. A band at the bottom (about 10-20% of the circumference) stays uncut. The passes clump together on either side of the gap instead of spreading evenly around the part. Heights (top_z, bottom_z) cover the whole part, and stock is flush with both ends.\n\nExpected:\nPasses spread evenly around the full 360 degrees of the cylinder circumference. No circumferential gap.\n\nEvidence:\nFound while machining the first-continuous-4axis-part example (Journal op, BN-0600 ball tool). Rotary Parallel generated 1629 moves with 1 warning. The toolpath covers about 80% of the circumference but leaves a gap at the bottom.\n\nDone means:\n- Rotary Parallel passes distribute evenly around the full 360 degree circumference of the model\n- No circumferential band stays uncut when top_z and bottom_z span the full part height\n- A screenshot of the gap is available (attached to this issue)\n\n<img width=\"2436\" height=\"1534\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d321bb2f-6c67-4074-87b6-78479e00fd4b\" />\n\n<img width=\"2352\" height=\"1506\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2477465-7574-4607-9775-d2b3ca8384c0\" />",
